 - L_i\\} + \\max\\{0, R_{i+1} - R_i\\}\\bigr)\\\\ & = ( \\pi(1)-1 + n-\\pi(1) ) + \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\bigl(\\max\\{0, \\pi(i+1)-\\pi(i)\\} + \\max\\{0, \\pi(i)-\\pi(i+1)\\}\\bigr)\\\\ & = (n-1) + \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\lvert \\pi(i+1)-\\pi(i) \\rvert. \\tag{3} \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nFor any permutation \\pi of \\{1,\\dots,n\\} each difference \\lvert \\pi(i+1)-\\pi(i) \\rvert is at least 1, so\n\n\\[ \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\lvert \\pi(i+1)-\\pi(i) \\rvert \\ge n-1. \\]\n\nSubstituting into (3) yields\n\n\\[ T \\ge (n-1)+(n-1)=2n-2. \\tag{4} \\]\n\nThus any tiling satisfying the condition uses at least 2n-2 tiles.\n\nWe now exhibit a tiling with exactly 2n-2 tiles. Choose the identity permutation \\pi(i)=i for all i. Then the left region D consists of all squares (i,j) with j<i (the strict lower triangle) and the right region C consists of all squares (i,j) with j>i (the strict upper triangle). For each row i (2 \\le i \\le n) place a horizontal 1\\times(i-1) tile covering the squares (i,1),\\dots,(i,i-1). This uses n-1 tiles and covers D completely. For each row i (1 \\le i \\le n-1) place a horizontal 1\\times(n-i) tile covering the squares (i,i+1),\\dots,(i,n). This uses another n-1 tiles and covers C completely. The n uncovered squares are precisely the diagonal squares (i,i). No tile contains an uncovered square, and every other unit square is covered exactly once. Hence a tiling with 2n-2 tiles exists.\n\nCombining the lower bound (4) with the construction, we conclude that the minimum possible number of tiles equals 2n-2. For n=2025 this value is\n\n\\[ 2\\cdot2025-2 = 4048. \\]\n\nThus the answer is 4048.\n\n### Self-Correction Instruction ###\n\nCheck that each step follows logically: the decomposition into left and right regions, the derivation of the lower bound (1) and (2) via the \u201cincrease\u201d argument, the algebraic simplification to (3), the use of \\lvert \\pi(i+1)-\\pi(i) \\rvert\\ge1, and the explicit construction for the identity permutation. Verify that no tile crosses an uncovered square and that all covered squares are accounted for. Ensure all LaTeX backslashes are escaped in the JSON output and that the final answer 4048 appears only in the \"final_answer\" field.",
